\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {On OLMo-3, the narrow solutions sit near the origin rather than on the left axis.} Each point is a model, placed by its general (x) and medical (y) misalignment rate; bars are binomial s.e.\ over 400 responses. Standard fine-tuning (blue) produces both kinds of misalignment. KL regularisation (orange; weights 0.7--30) removes general misalignment but most of the medical misalignment with it. Hollow diamonds are \citeauthor  {soligo2026easy}'s Fig.~3 values for Qwen-14B (GPT-4o judge), whose narrow solutions keep 31--51\% medical misalignment. Our judge reports misalignment about 1.7$\times $ as often, so only the shape is comparable.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frontier}{{2}{4}{\textbf {On OLMo-3, the narrow solutions sit near the origin rather than on the left axis.} Each point is a model, placed by its general (x) and medical (y) misalignment rate; bars are binomial s.e.\ over 400 responses. Standard fine-tuning (blue) produces both kinds of misalignment. KL regularisation (orange; weights 0.7--30) removes general misalignment but most of the medical misalignment with it. Hollow diamonds are \citeauthor {soligo2026easy}'s Fig.~3 values for Qwen-14B (GPT-4o judge), whose narrow solutions keep 31--51\% medical misalignment. Our judge reports misalignment about 1.7$\times $ as often, so only the shape is comparable}{figure.2}{}}
